<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Aerodesign on Jesús Vargas Portfolio</title><link>https://jmvargascruz.github.io/categories/aerodesign/</link><description>Recent content in Aerodesign on Jesús Vargas Portfolio</description><generator>Hugo -- gohugo.io</generator><language>en</language><lastBuildDate>Mon, 01 Jan 2024 00:00:00 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://jmvargascruz.github.io/categories/aerodesign/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Cloud Surfer 2022 | Aerodesign</title><link>https://jmvargascruz.github.io/projects/cloud-surfer-aerodesign/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 2024 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://jmvargascruz.github.io/projects/cloud-surfer-aerodesign/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="overview"&gt;Overview&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Cloud Surfer 2022 was a radio-controlled cargo aircraft developed as part of the SAE Aerodesign Mexico competition. The project focused on aerodynamic optimization, structural feasibility, and payload integration within competition constraints.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="tools-and-technologies"&gt;Tools and Technologies&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;SolidWorks for 3D modeling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ansys Fluent for CFD simulation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;XFLR5 for preliminary aerodynamic analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;MATLAB for performance estimation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
